        "result": "Implementation complete.\n\n**Changed paths**\n- `ref_lab/evidence_gate/checker.py` — added step 0 to `ProgrammaticChecker.audit()` plus a new `_check_substantive_research_present()` helper (also noted in the module docstring).\n- `tests/test_research_evidence_gate.py` — added four regression tests and two package factories; docstring item 13.\n- `ref_lab/evidence_gate/loop.py` — **not modified** (not needed; the fix belongs in the checker).\n\n**Technical cause**\n`ProgrammaticChecker.audit()` had no presence check: every audit rule is a loop over `package.sources`, `package.media_artifacts`, or `package.claims`. With `claims=[]` (and even `sources=[]`), those loops execute zero iterations and return zero issues, so `QualityGateLoop.evaluate()` found `error_issues == []` and took the PASS branch, minting a real `AdmissionReceipt` with `total_claims_verified=0` and writing `ADMISSION_RECEIPT.json`. Absent evidence was indistinguishable from clean evidence.\n\n**Fix**\nThe checker now emits a Tier1 `AuditIssue` with `issue_code=\"EMPTY_RESEARCH_EVIDENCE\"`, `severity=\"ERROR\"`, `field=\"claims\"` whenever `package.claims` is empty, with distinct messages for a fully empty package vs. a sources-and/or-media-only package (the latter names source/media counts and states metadata alone is not substantive research). Consequences flow through existing semantics unchanged: cycle 1 → REVISE with a `REWORK_PACKAGE.json` and no receipt; at `cycle >= max_cycles` → BLOCKED, still no receipt. Schemas are untouched, so incomplete input still parses and yields gate feedback rather than an input-validation exception. Nonempty packages take the same path as before, so media-integrity checks, semantic audit, cycle cap, and export behavior are all preserved.\n\n**Test status: NOT RUN.** I have no shell/test runner in this session, so nothing here is verified by execution. The new tests are unexecuted; the existing ones were not re-run and were not modified or weakened. Codex's independent acceptance suite was not read or touched. New tests assert for both empty and sources-only packages: `decision != \"PASS\"` (and `== \"REVISE\"`), `receipt is None`, a rework package carrying the ERROR issue, export producing `REWORK_PACKAGE.json` and no `ADMISSION_RECEIPT.json`; plus BLOCKED at the cycle cap, and a PASS with `total_claims_verified == 1` for the real single-claim package with temporary-file fixture hashing.",
